plugin-hostd (0.12.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * ci: the deb install job takes the channel's contract data packages; the
    fuzz mutant cites protocol.h:53
  * plugin-hostd-contract depends on omx-clap-core-contract
  * One name per refusal number: the shared ones are omx-clap-core's
    reply.host.*
  * release: plugin-hostd 0.12.0
  * README: the daemon's verbs are declared in its contract directory
  * Hold the declared verbs to the daemon on its socket
  * The instance-unknown refusal is -3, the number the daemon answers
  * Ship the contract directory's files in a noarch plugin-hostd-contract
    package
  * Read the daemon's own verbs from the rendered header, not from protocol.h
  * Declare the daemon's own verbs and reply codes in its contract directory

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:23:21 +0000
